Task: Build a dedicated native iOS “BlueMind Photos” picker/gallery inside BlueMind.

This is not just a visual wrapper around the current system picker.

I want BlueMind to have its own polished in-app photo selection experience, while still reading the user’s real iPhone photo library through native iOS APIs.

Use PhotoKit / Photos framework for library access and asset loading.

The picker should be iOS-only and must not modify Web behavior.

⸻

MAIN GOAL

Create a dedicated BlueMind Photos experience that can show:

* old photos;
* newly taken photos;
* screenshots;
* saved images;
* camera photos;
* albums / collections;
* any other Photos-library assets the user has granted access to.

This should NOT be limited to photos taken from BlueMind’s own camera.

It should reflect the user’s actual iPhone Photos library according to the permission level granted to BlueMind.

⸻

VISUAL DIRECTION

The UI should feel:

* native iOS;
* modern;
* compact;
* smooth;
* premium;
* clearly part of BlueMind.

Do not blindly copy another app.

Build a BlueMind-native implementation using real iOS materials and controls where possible.

