⸻

SPEED / THUMBNAILS

The photo picker should feel immediate.

Use lightweight cached thumbnails for the grid.

Do not load original 4K/full-resolution image data just to display the grid.

However:

when the user confirms selected images, BlueMind must preserve access to the original/highest-quality asset for:

* sending;
* upload;
* fullscreen preview;
* image analysis.

Keep these responsibilities separate:

Grid thumbnail = lightweight

Attachment source = original/highest quality

Never permanently replace an original asset with the thumbnail.

⸻

ICLOUD PHOTOS

Handle iCloud-backed Photos assets correctly.

Some originals may not exist locally.

Requirements:

* show the thumbnail if available;
* resolve/download original asset when required;
* show a meaningful processing/loading state;
* never freeze indefinitely;
* handle network/error cases.

Do not block the whole picker while one iCloud image downloads.

⸻

PERMISSIONS

Use the real iOS Photos authorization flow.

Support:

* full library access;
* limited Photos access;
* denied access.

If access is limited:

show only the assets iOS allows BlueMind to access.

If permission is denied:

provide a clean native explanation/state and appropriate path to Settings if needed.

Do not bypass iOS privacy behavior.

⸻

CAMERA INTEGRATION

BlueMind already has its own native camera flow.

Keep it separate but integrated.

From BlueMind Photos, optionally provide a clear camera entry point if appropriate.

If the user takes a new photo through the BlueMind camera:

* that captured photo should still be able to appear in the user’s Photos library if the existing product flow saves it there;
* BlueMind Photos should refresh/update naturally afterward.

Do not create duplicate internal attachments.

⸻

SEARCH

If practical with the current architecture, leave room for future search/filter.

But do not delay the first implementation by inventing AI photo search right now.

Core gallery selection must come first.

⸻

FULLSCREEN PREVIEW

When tapping/long-pressing for preview if we support preview from this gallery:

* use the original/highest-quality asset;
* do not use the grid thumbnail as final fullscreen source;
* preserve aspect ratio;
* support zoom/pan if preview exists.

Do not regress the image-quality work we already did.

⸻

PERFORMANCE

Use efficient native image-library APIs.

Specifically consider:

* PHFetchResult
* PHAsset
* PHCachingImageManager
* lazy loading
* preheating/caching around visible cells
* cancellation of offscreen image requests

Avoid:

* loading full-resolution images for the whole grid;
* base64 conversion for every thumbnail;
* blocking the main thread;
* unnecessary duplicate decoding;
* repeated full-library reloads.

⸻

IOS ONLY

Do not modify:

* Web photo picker;
* backend;
* unrelated composer logic;
* voice system;
* transcription;
* AI model selector;
* existing camera capture quality.

If shared code exists, isolate BlueMind Photos to the iOS presentation/data path.

